Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-ecm: stop the module-reload and emesh-classifier boot noise

The v89-2 boot log of the SBE1V1K carries five error lines that all come
from /etc/init.d/qca-nss-ecm (qca/feeds/nss/clients/qca-nss-ecm):

  daemon.err rmmod: unloading the module failed
  daemon.err insmod: module is already loaded - qca-nss-sfe
  daemon.err insmod: module is already loaded - qca-wifi-nss-plugins
  procd: /etc/rc.d/S26qca-nss-ecm: ... can't create
      /proc/sys/net/ecm/ecm_classifier_emesh/enabled: nonexistent directory
  procd: /etc/rc.d/S26qca-nss-ecm: ... can't create
      /proc/sys/net/ecm/ecm_classifier_emesh/sawf_enabled: nonexistent directory

None of them changes what the script accomplishes; each is a call that
cannot succeed on this image.

1. load_sfe() reloads qca-nss-sfe to apply sixth_tuple_enable, but
   /etc/modules.d/09-qca-nss-sfe already has kmodloader load the module
   before S26 runs.  Something still holds a reference (on the v89-2
   boot: pppoe/ppp_generic and ecm's dependency list), so rmmod fails and
   the unconditional insmod behind it can only answer "module is already
   loaded".  Try the unload quietly and issue the insmod only when the
   module actually came out.  When the unload fails the module keeps the
   parameters it was loaded with -- exactly the outcome the current code
   gets, minus the two error lines.

2. load_ecm()'s plugin guard is one &&/|| list:

     [ -d /sys/module/qca_wifi_nss_plugins ] || [ -f /tmp/.wifi-config-done ] ||
     [ -f /lib/modules/$kernel_version/ath.ko ] && insmod qca-wifi-nss-plugins

   && and || have equal precedence and associate left, so this reads
   ((A || B) || C) && insmod.  ath.ko exists in this image, which makes
   the whole chain true on every boot, so the plugins are insmodded even
   when /sys/module/qca_wifi_nss_plugins is present.  Write the guard out
   as the intended conjunction: load only when the plugins are not loaded
   yet and wifi has not taken over the stack (/tmp/.wifi-config-done).

3. start() writes the SAWF and EMESH classifier knobs unconditionally.
   This build does not include the mesh classifier, so the
   ecm_classifier_emesh directory never exists and both writes fail.
   Test the directory first; nothing changes on a build that has it.

---

--- a/qca/feeds/nss/clients/qca-nss-ecm/files/qca-nss-ecm.init	2026-11-16 02:22:25.081494366 +0000
+++ b/qca/feeds/nss/clients/qca-nss-ecm/files/qca-nss-ecm.init	2026-11-16 02:22:49.185623493 +0000
@@ -95,11 +95,18 @@
 	local kernel_version=$(uname -r)
 
 	[ -e "/lib/modules/$kernel_version/qca-nss-sfe.ko" ] && {
-		[ -d /sys/module/qca_nss_sfe ] && rmmod qca-nss-sfe
-		if [ $(get_sixth_tuple_mode) == 0 ]; then
-			insmod qca-nss-sfe
-		else
-			insmod qca-nss-sfe sixth_tuple_enable=1
+		# kmodloader already loads qca-nss-sfe from /etc/modules.d before this
+		# script runs.  The module is held by its users and refuses to unload;
+		# the insmod that used to follow unconditionally then only printed
+		# "module is already loaded" on every boot.  Reload it only when the
+		# unload actually succeeded.
+		[ -d /sys/module/qca_nss_sfe ] && rmmod qca-nss-sfe 2>/dev/null
+		if [ ! -d /sys/module/qca_nss_sfe ]; then
+			if [ $(get_sixth_tuple_mode) == 0 ]; then
+				insmod qca-nss-sfe
+			else
+				insmod qca-nss-sfe sixth_tuple_enable=1
+			fi
 		fi
 	}
 
@@ -150,10 +157,18 @@
 
 	local kernel_version=$(uname -r)
 
-	[ -e "/lib/modules/$kernel_version/qca-wifi-nss-plugins.ko" ] && {
-		[ -d /sys/module/qca_wifi_nss_plugins ] || [ -f /tmp/.wifi-config-done ] ||
-		[ -f /lib/modules/$kernel_version/ath.ko ] && insmod qca-wifi-nss-plugins
-	}
+	# The old condition chained && and || into one list, so the trailing
+	# "&& insmod" ran whenever the last test (ath.ko exists) was true --
+	# including the case where the plugin module was already loaded, which
+	# only produced "module is already loaded" at boot.  Spell the guard out:
+	# load the plugins only when they are not loaded yet and wifi is still
+	# under this script's control.
+	if [ -e "/lib/modules/$kernel_version/qca-wifi-nss-plugins.ko" ] &&
+		[ ! -d /sys/module/qca_wifi_nss_plugins ] &&
+		[ ! -f /tmp/.wifi-config-done ] &&
+		[ -f /lib/modules/$kernel_version/ath.ko ]; then
+		insmod qca-wifi-nss-plugins
+	fi
 
 	echo 0 > /sys/kernel/debug/ecm/front_end_ipv4_stop
 	echo 0 > /sys/kernel/debug/ecm/front_end_ipv6_stop
@@ -224,9 +239,13 @@
 		insmod ecm_ovs
 	fi
 
-	# Enable SAWF and EMESH classifier by default for Out-of box prioritization
-	echo 3 > /proc/sys/net/ecm/ecm_classifier_emesh/enabled
-	echo 3 > /proc/sys/net/ecm/ecm_classifier_emesh/sawf_enabled
+	# Enable SAWF and EMESH classifier by default for Out-of box prioritization.
+	# ecm_classifier_emesh only exists when the build includes the mesh
+	# classifier; without it both writes fail with "nonexistent directory".
+	if [ -d /proc/sys/net/ecm/ecm_classifier_emesh ]; then
+		echo 3 > /proc/sys/net/ecm/ecm_classifier_emesh/enabled
+		echo 3 > /proc/sys/net/ecm/ecm_classifier_emesh/sawf_enabled
+	fi
 
 	# If UDP classifier is present, start it.
 	[ -f /etc/init.d/udp-clf ] && /etc/init.d/udp-clf start
